#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""ctlhq-env: start, snapshot, restore, and drive test machines with one command set.

Usage:
  ctlhq-env [options] list
  ctlhq-env [options] up NAME
  ctlhq-env [options] down NAME
  ctlhq-env [options] snapshot NAME TAG
  ctlhq-env [options] restore NAME TAG
  ctlhq-env [options] exec NAME -- CMD [ARG ...]
  ctlhq-env [options] screenshot NAME --out FILE
  ctlhq-env [options] status NAME

Options (anywhere before `--`):
  --provider P   local, fake, tart, or utm (default: the recipe's provider)
  --json         print one JSON object (list: a JSON array) instead of text
  --envs DIR     the recipe folder (default: envs/ next to this tool's bin/)
  --state DIR    where logs and fake state live (default: .local/env/ in the
                 repository; the CTLHQ_ENV_STATE variable also sets it)

NAME is a recipe, envs/NAME.toml. The machine has the same name as the recipe.

Commands:
  list        number every recipe: name, provider, guest, image, summary. With
              --provider it also asks that provider once for each machine's state.
  up          create the machine from the image when it is absent, start it, wait
              for its IP address, and run the recipe's provision commands on a new
              machine. It prints what the recipe does not cover.
  down        stop the machine. The machine and its snapshots stay.
  snapshot    save the machine's disks under TAG. A second snapshot with the same
              TAG replaces the first.
  restore     put the machine back to TAG.
  exec        run CMD in the machine and return CMD's own exit code. Output passes
              through; with --json it is captured into the JSON object.
  screenshot  run the recipe's screenshot_cmd in the machine (it prints a base64
              PNG), decode it, and write FILE. A recipe without one exits 1.
  status      the machine's state (absent, stopped, running) and IP address.

Providers:
  local   runs commands on this machine. up and down do nothing and say so;
          snapshot and restore exit 1; screenshot uses screencapture.
  fake    runs nothing. It keeps machine state in <state>/fake/state.json, adds
          one JSON line per call to <state>/fake/calls.jsonl, and prints the steps
          the recipe's real provider would take. A scripted result comes from
          <state>/fake/script.json: {"<command>": {"exit": N, "stdout": "...",
          "stderr": "..."}}. A scripted non-zero exit leaves the state unchanged.
          exec and screenshot need a running fake machine.
  tart    Tart, for macOS and Linux guests. UNPROVEN UNTIL THE HOST: written from
          Tart's public documentation and source, tested only against a fake tart.
          up: tart list --format json; tart clone IMAGE NAME; tart set NAME --cpu C
          --memory M --disk-size D; tart run --no-graphics [network flag] NAME (in
          the background, output in <state>/logs/); tart ip NAME --wait 120.
          A snapshot is a local clone named NAME-snap-TAG (copy-on-write on APFS,
          disks only); the machine is stopped for the copy and started again.
          restore deletes NAME and clones NAME-snap-TAG back to NAME.
          exec: tart exec NAME CMD (needs the Tart Guest Agent in the guest).
  utm     UTM's utmctl, for Windows and other guests. UNPROVEN UNTIL THE HOST:
          written from UTM's public documentation and utmctl source, tested only
          against a fake utmctl. utmctl cannot create machines or set CPU, memory,
          disk, or network, so the recipe's image names a UTM machine to clone.
          up: utmctl status NAME; utmctl clone IMAGE --name NAME; utmctl start NAME
          --hide; utmctl ip-address NAME (retried until CTLHQ_ENV_WAIT seconds).
          snapshot: utmctl snapshot list NAME --json, then snapshot create NAME
          --name TAG, or snapshot overwrite NAME --snapshot TAG. restore: utmctl
          snapshot restore NAME --snapshot TAG (UTM 5.0.6 or later). exec: utmctl
          exec NAME --cmd CMD. utmctl needs the logged-in desktop session, not SSH.
          utmctl is found as CTLHQ_ENV_UTMCTL, on PATH, or in /Applications/UTM.app.
  A provider binary that is missing exits 127 with an install hint. CTLHQ_ENV_TART
  names a tart binary to use instead of the one on PATH.

Recipes (envs/<name>.toml, a small TOML subset: strings, integers, booleans,
arrays, comments):
  required  name, summary, provider (tart, utm, or local), guest (linux, macos,
            windows), image, cpu, memory_mb, disk_gb, network (shared, softnet,
            or bridged:<interface>), not_covered (a non-empty array of strings)
  optional  user, root, snapshot_before_risky, provision (shell commands run once
            on a new machine), screenshot_cmd, services, log, notes
  Linux and macOS commands run as `sh -c CMD`; Windows commands as
  `powershell.exe -NoProfile -NonInteractive -Command CMD`. Tart refuses a
  disk_gb below the image's own disk size.

Environment: CTLHQ_ENV_STATE (state folder), CTLHQ_ENV_WAIT (seconds to wait
for an IP address, default 120), CTLHQ_ENV_TIMEOUT (seconds per provider call,
default 900), CTLHQ_ENV_RUN_GRACE (seconds to watch a background `tart run`
for an early failure, default 3).

Exit codes: 0 success; 1 a problem (absent machine, unknown TAG, no screenshot
command, bad recipe); 2 a usage error; 127 a provider binary is missing. When a
provider call fails, ctlhq-env names the call and exits with that call's own
exit code. exec exits with CMD's exit code.

Rule encoded (AGENTS.md): "Keep blocked operations, working local actions, and
missing evidence separate in totals." The fake provider says "fake provider" on
every result and never reports a machine as started.

Sources:
  https://tart.run/quick-start/
  https://github.com/cirruslabs/tart/tree/main/Sources/tart/Commands
    (Clone.swift, Run.swift, Set.swift, Stop.swift, Delete.swift, List.swift,
    IP.swift, Exec.swift; read for Tart 2.41.1, 2026-10-17)
  https://docs.getutm.app/scripting/scripting/
  https://github.com/utmapp/UTM/blob/v5.0.8/utmctl/UTMCtl.swift
    (utmctl --help text; read for UTM 5.0.8, 2026-10-17)
"""
from __future__ import annotations

import base64
import json
import os
import re
import shlex
import shutil
import socket
import subprocess
import sys
import time
from pathlib import Path

ROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent
NAME_RE = re.compile(r"^[A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9._-]*$")
PROVIDERS = ("local", "fake", "tart", "utm")
COMMANDS = ("list", "up", "down", "snapshot", "restore", "exec", "screenshot", "status")
PNG_MAGIC = b"\x89PNG\r\n\x1a\n"
TINY_PNG = base64.b64decode(
    "iVBORw0KGgoAAAANSUhEUgAAAAEAAAABCAYAAAAfFcSJAAAADUlEQVR42mNkYPhfDwAChwGA60e6kgAAAABJRU5ErkJggg=="
)
USAGE = "usage: ctlhq-env [--provider P] [--json] [--envs DIR] [--state DIR] list|up|down|snapshot|restore|exec|screenshot|status ..."


class Fail(Exception):
    def __init__(self, msg: str, code: int = 1) -> None:
        super().__init__(msg)
        self.msg = msg
        self.code = code


class Usage(Exception):
    pass


def env_float(key: str, default: float) -> float:
    try:
        return float(os.environ.get(key, default))
    except ValueError:
        return default


class TomlError(Exception):
    pass


class _Toml:
    """The TOML subset that recipes use; Python 3.9 has no tomllib."""

    def __init__(self, text: str) -> None:
        self.t = text
        self.i = 0
        self.line = 1

    def err(self, msg: str):
        raise TomlError(f"line {self.line}: {msg}")

    def peek(self) -> str:
        return self.t[self.i] if self.i < len(self.t) else ""

    def adv(self) -> str:
        c = self.t[self.i]
        self.i += 1
        if c == "\n":
            self.line += 1
        return c

    def skip(self, newlines: bool = False) -> None:
        while True:
            c = self.peek()
            if c in (" ", "\t", "\r"):
                self.adv()
            elif c == "#":
                while self.peek() not in ("", "\n"):
                    self.adv()
            elif newlines and c == "\n":
                self.adv()
            else:
                return

    def doc(self) -> dict:
        root: dict = {}
        cur = root
        while True:
            self.skip(newlines=True)
            if self.peek() == "":
                return root
            if self.peek() == "[":
                self.adv()
                key = self.key()
                self.skip()
                if self.peek() != "]":
                    self.err("expected ] after the table name")
                self.adv()
                if key in root:
                    self.err(f"[{key}] is defined twice")
                cur = root[key] = {}
            else:
                key = self.key()
                self.skip()
                if self.peek() != "=":
                    self.err(f"expected = after {key}")
                self.adv()
                self.skip()
                if key in cur:
                    self.err(f"{key} is set twice")
                cur[key] = self.value()
            self.skip()
            if self.peek() not in ("", "\n"):
                self.err("unexpected text after the value")

    def key(self) -> str:
        self.skip()
        start = self.i
        while self.peek() and (self.peek().isalnum() or self.peek() in "_-"):
            self.adv()
        if self.i == start:
            self.err("expected a key")
        return self.t[start:self.i]

    def value(self):
        c = self.peek()
        if c == '"':
            return self.basic()
        if c == "'":
            return self.literal()
        if c == "[":
            return self.array()
        start = self.i
        while self.peek() and self.peek() not in " \t\r\n#,]":
            self.adv()
        word = self.t[start:self.i]
        if word == "true":
            return True
        if word == "false":
            return False
        if re.fullmatch(r"[+-]?[0-9]+", word):
            return int(word)
        self.err(f"unsupported value {word!r}: use a string, an integer, true, false, or an array")

    def basic(self) -> str:
        self.adv()
        out = []
        escapes = {"n": "\n", "t": "\t", '"': '"', "\\": "\\"}
        while True:
            c = self.peek()
            if c in ("", "\n"):
                self.err("unterminated string")
            self.adv()
            if c == '"':
                return "".join(out)
            if c == "\\":
                e = self.peek()
                if e not in escapes:
                    self.err(f"unsupported escape \\{e}")
                self.adv()
                out.append(escapes[e])
            else:
                out.append(c)

    def literal(self) -> str:
        self.adv()
        start = self.i
        while self.peek() != "'":
            if self.peek() in ("", "\n"):
                self.err("unterminated string")
            self.adv()
        s = self.t[start:self.i]
        self.adv()
        return s

    def array(self) -> list:
        self.adv()
        items = []
        while True:
            self.skip(newlines=True)
            if self.peek() == "]":
                self.adv()
                return items
            if self.peek() == "":
                self.err("unterminated array")
            items.append(self.value())
            self.skip(newlines=True)
            if self.peek() == ",":
                self.adv()
            elif self.peek() != "]":
                self.err("expected , or ] in the array")


def parse_toml(text: str) -> dict:
    return _Toml(text).doc()


REQUIRED = {
    "name": str, "summary": str, "provider": str, "guest": str, "image": str,
    "cpu": int, "memory_mb": int, "disk_gb": int, "network": str, "not_covered": list,
}
OPTIONAL = {
    "user": str, "root": bool, "snapshot_before_risky": bool, "provision": list,
    "screenshot_cmd": str, "services": list, "log": str, "notes": str,
}


def check_recipe(data: dict, stem: str) -> list:
    problems = []
    for key, kind in {**REQUIRED, **OPTIONAL}.items():
        if key not in data:
            if key in REQUIRED:
                problems.append(f"missing {key}")
            continue
        v = data[key]
        if type(v) is not kind:
            problems.append(f"{key} must be {kind.__name__}")
        elif kind is list and not all(isinstance(x, str) and x.strip() for x in v):
            problems.append(f"{key} must hold non-empty strings")
    for key in data:
        if key not in REQUIRED and key not in OPTIONAL:
            problems.append(f"unknown key {key}")
    if problems:
        return problems
    if data["name"] != stem:
        problems.append(f"name {data['name']!r} differs from the file name {stem!r}")
    if data["provider"] not in ("tart", "utm", "local"):
        problems.append("provider must be tart, utm, or local")
    if data["guest"] not in ("linux", "macos", "windows"):
        problems.append("guest must be linux, macos, or windows")
    if data["provider"] == "tart" and data["guest"] == "windows":
        problems.append("tart runs macOS and Linux guests only; use utm")
    net = data["network"]
    if not (net in ("shared", "softnet") or re.fullmatch(r"bridged:[A-Za-z0-9._-]+", net)):
        problems.append("network must be shared, softnet, or bridged:<interface>")
    for key in ("cpu", "memory_mb", "disk_gb"):
        if data[key] <= 0:
            problems.append(f"{key} must be above 0")
    if not data["not_covered"]:
        problems.append("not_covered must name at least one thing")
    return problems


def load_recipe(envs: Path, name: str) -> dict:
    if not NAME_RE.match(name):
        raise Usage(f"bad machine name {name!r}")
    path = envs / f"{name}.toml"
    if not path.is_file():
        known = ", ".join(sorted(p.stem for p in envs.glob("*.toml"))) or "none"
        raise Fail(f"no recipe {path} (recipes: {known})", 1)
    try:
        data = parse_toml(path.read_text(encoding="utf-8"))
    except TomlError as e:
        raise Fail(f"{path}: {e}", 1)
    problems = check_recipe(data, name)
    if problems:
        raise Fail(f"{path}: " + "; ".join(problems), 1)
    data["_path"] = str(path)
    return data


def all_recipes(envs: Path) -> list:
    return [load_recipe(envs, p.stem) for p in sorted(envs.glob("*.toml"))]


def guest_shell(recipe: dict, cmd: str) -> list:
    if recipe["guest"] == "windows":
        return [r"C:\Windows\System32\WindowsPowerShell\v1.0\powershell.exe",
                "-NoProfile", "-NonInteractive", "-Command", cmd]
    return ["sh", "-c", cmd]


def show(argv: list) -> str:
    return shlex.join(str(a) for a in argv)


class StepFailed(Fail):
    pass


class Provider:
    """Shared plumbing. With `assume` set (a FakeState), calls are only recorded,
    and state questions are answered from that fake state: the plan of a real run."""

    binary = ""
    install_hint = ""
    env_override = ""

    def __init__(self, recipe: dict, ctx: dict, assume=None) -> None:
        self.r = recipe
        self.name = recipe["name"]
        self.ctx = ctx
        self.assume = assume
        self.steps: list = []
        self.notes: list = []
        self.ip = ""

    def exe(self) -> str:
        override = os.environ.get(self.env_override, "") if self.env_override else ""
        if override:
            if os.path.isfile(override) and os.access(override, os.X_OK):
                return override
            raise Fail(f"{self.binary} not found at {override} ({self.env_override}). {self.install_hint}", 127)
        found = shutil.which(self.binary) or self.fallback()
        if not found:
            raise Fail(f"{self.binary} not found on PATH. {self.install_hint}", 127)
        return found

    def fallback(self) -> str:
        return ""

    def say(self, line: str) -> None:
        if not self.ctx["json"]:
            print(line, file=sys.stderr, flush=True)

    def call(self, args: list, passthrough: bool = False, check: bool = True):
        argv = [self.binary] + args
        if self.assume is not None:
            self.steps.append({"argv": argv, "exit": None})
            return 0, "", ""
        exe = self.exe()
        n = len(self.steps) + 1
        timeout = env_float("CTLHQ_ENV_TIMEOUT", 900)
        try:
            if passthrough:
                p = subprocess.run([exe] + args, timeout=timeout)
                out, err = "", ""
            else:
                p = subprocess.run([exe] + args, capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=timeout,
                                   stdin=subprocess.DEVNULL)
                out, err = p.stdout, p.stderr
        except subprocess.TimeoutExpired:
            self.steps.append({"argv": argv, "exit": "timeout"})
            raise Fail(f"step {n} timed out after {timeout:g} s: {show(argv)}", 1)
        self.steps.append({"argv": argv, "exit": p.returncode})
        if check and p.returncode != 0:
            raise StepFailed(f"step {n} failed: {show(argv)} exited {p.returncode}"
                             + (f": {err.strip()[-400:]}" if err.strip() else ""), p.returncode)
        return p.returncode, out, err

    def spawn(self, args: list) -> None:
        argv = [self.binary] + args
        if self.assume is not None:
            self.steps.append({"argv": argv, "exit": None, "background": True})
            return
        exe = self.exe()
        n = len(self.steps) + 1
        logs = self.ctx["state"] / "logs"
        logs.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
        log = logs / f"{self.name}-{self.binary}-run.log"
        with open(log, "ab") as fh:
            p = subprocess.Popen([exe] + args, stdin=subprocess.DEVNULL, stdout=fh,
                                 stderr=subprocess.STDOUT, start_new_session=True)
        try:
            rc = p.wait(timeout=env_float("CTLHQ_ENV_RUN_GRACE", 3))
        except subprocess.TimeoutExpired:
            rc = None
        self.steps.append({"argv": argv, "exit": "running" if rc is None else rc, "background": True, "log": str(log)})
        if rc not in (None, 0):
            tail = log.read_text(encoding="utf-8", errors="replace").strip()[-400:]
            raise StepFailed(f"step {n} failed: {show(argv)} exited {rc}" + (f": {tail}" if tail else ""), rc)

    def provision(self) -> None:
        for cmd in self.r.get("provision", []):
            self.call(self.exec_args(guest_shell(self.r, cmd)))

    def screenshot(self, out: Path) -> None:
        cmd = self.r.get("screenshot_cmd")
        if not cmd:
            raise Fail(f"recipe {self.name} has no screenshot_cmd (see its not_covered list)", 1)
        _, text, _ = self.call(self.exec_args(guest_shell(self.r, cmd)))
        if self.assume is not None:
            return
        try:
            data = base64.b64decode("".join(text.split()), validate=True)
        except ValueError:
            raise Fail("screenshot_cmd did not print base64", 1)
        if not data.startswith(PNG_MAGIC):
            raise Fail("screenshot_cmd output is not a PNG image", 1)
        out.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
        out.write_bytes(data)

    def exec(self, argv: list):
        passthrough = not self.ctx["json"]
        rc, out, err = self.call(self.exec_args(argv), passthrough=passthrough, check=False)
        return rc, out, err

    def require(self, state: str, allowed: tuple, what: str) -> None:
        if state not in allowed:
            raise Fail(f"{self.name} is {state}; {what}", 1)


class Tart(Provider):
    binary = "tart"
    install_hint = "Install it with: brew install cirruslabs/cli/tart (https://tart.run/quick-start/)"
    env_override = "CTLHQ_ENV_TART"

    def snap(self, tag: str) -> str:
        return f"{self.name}-snap-{tag}"

    def machines(self) -> dict:
        _, out, _ = self.call(["list", "--format", "json"])
        if self.assume is not None:
            return self.assume.as_tart(self.name)
        try:
            rows = json.loads(out or "[]")
        except ValueError:
            raise Fail("tart list --format json did not print JSON", 1)
        found = {}
        for row in rows if isinstance(rows, list) else []:
            if not isinstance(row, dict) or str(row.get("Source", "local")).lower() != "local":
                continue
            running = row.get("Running") is True or str(row.get("State", "")).lower() == "running"
            found[str(row.get("Name", ""))] = "running" if running else "stopped"
        return found

    def state(self) -> str:
        return self.machines().get(self.name, "absent")

    def tags(self, machines: dict) -> list:
        prefix = self.snap("")
        return sorted(n[len(prefix):] for n in machines if n.startswith(prefix))

    def net_flags(self) -> list:
        net = self.r["network"]
        if net == "softnet":
            return ["--net-softnet"]
        if net.startswith("bridged:"):
            return [f"--net-bridged={net.split(':', 1)[1]}"]
        return []

    def start(self) -> None:
        self.spawn(["run", "--no-graphics"] + self.net_flags() + [self.name])
        wait = int(env_float("CTLHQ_ENV_WAIT", 120))
        _, out, _ = self.call(["ip", self.name, "--wait", str(wait)])
        self.ip = out.strip().splitlines()[0] if out.strip() else ""

    def stop(self) -> None:
        self.call(["stop", "--timeout", "60", self.name])

    def up(self) -> str:
        state = self.state()
        fresh = state == "absent"
        if fresh:
            self.call(["clone", self.r["image"], self.name])
            self.call(["set", self.name, "--cpu", str(self.r["cpu"]), "--memory", str(self.r["memory_mb"]),
                       "--disk-size", str(self.r["disk_gb"])])
        if state == "running":
            self.notes.append(f"{self.name} was already running")
            _, out, _ = self.call(["ip", self.name])
            self.ip = out.strip().splitlines()[0] if out.strip() else ""
        else:
            self.start()
        if fresh:
            self.provision()
        return "running"

    def down(self) -> str:
        state = self.state()
        self.require(state, ("running", "stopped"), "there is nothing to stop")
        if state == "running":
            self.stop()
        else:
            self.notes.append(f"{self.name} was already stopped")
        return "stopped"

    def snapshot(self, tag: str) -> str:
        machines = self.machines()
        state = machines.get(self.name, "absent")
        self.require(state, ("running", "stopped"), "run `ctlhq-env up` first")
        if state == "running":
            self.stop()
        if tag in self.tags(machines):
            self.call(["delete", self.snap(tag)])
            self.notes.append(f"replaced the earlier snapshot {tag}")
        self.call(["clone", self.name, self.snap(tag)])
        if state == "running":
            self.start()
        return state

    def restore(self, tag: str) -> str:
        machines = self.machines()
        state = machines.get(self.name, "absent")
        if tag not in self.tags(machines):
            raise Fail(f"{self.name} has no snapshot {tag!r} (snapshots: {', '.join(self.tags(machines)) or 'none'})", 1)
        if state == "running":
            self.stop()
        if state != "absent":
            self.call(["delete", self.name])
        self.call(["clone", self.snap(tag), self.name])
        if state == "running":
            self.start()
        return "stopped" if state == "absent" else state

    def exec_args(self, argv: list) -> list:
        return ["exec", self.name] + argv

    def status(self) -> str:
        state = self.state()
        if state == "running":
            rc, out, _ = self.call(["ip", self.name], check=False)
            self.ip = out.strip().splitlines()[0] if rc == 0 and out.strip() else ""
        return state

    def list_states(self) -> dict:
        return self.machines()


class Utm(Provider):
    binary = "utmctl"
    install_hint = ("Install UTM 5.0.6 or later from https://mac.getutm.app, then link it: "
                    "sudo ln -s /Applications/UTM.app/Contents/MacOS/utmctl /usr/local/bin/utmctl")
    env_override = "CTLHQ_ENV_UTMCTL"
    BUNDLED = "/Applications/UTM.app/Contents/MacOS/utmctl"
    STOPPED = ("stopped",)

    def fallback(self) -> str:
        return self.BUNDLED if os.access(self.BUNDLED, os.X_OK) else ""

    def state(self) -> str:
        rc, out, _ = self.call(["status", self.name], check=False)
        if self.assume is not None:
            return self.assume.machine_state(self.name)
        if rc != 0:
            return "absent"
        word = out.strip().split()[0] if out.strip() else "unknown"
        return "stopped" if word in self.STOPPED else ("running" if word == "started" else word)

    def wait_ip(self) -> None:
        deadline = time.monotonic() + env_float("CTLHQ_ENV_WAIT", 120)
        while True:
            rc, out, err = self.call(["ip-address", self.name], check=False)
            if rc == 0 and (out.strip() or self.assume is not None):
                self.ip = out.strip().splitlines()[0] if out.strip() else ""
                return
            if time.monotonic() >= deadline:
                raise StepFailed(f"step {len(self.steps)} failed: utmctl ip-address {self.name} exited {rc}"
                                 + (f": {err.strip()[-400:]}" if err.strip() else " with no address"), rc or 1)
            time.sleep(4)

    def up(self) -> str:
        state = self.state()
        fresh = state == "absent"
        if fresh:
            self.call(["clone", self.r["image"], "--name", self.name])
            self.notes.append(f"utmctl cannot set CPU, memory, disk, or network; the template {self.r['image']} holds them "
                              f"(recipe: {self.r['cpu']} CPU, {self.r['memory_mb']} MB, {self.r['disk_gb']} GB, {self.r['network']})")
        if state == "running":
            self.notes.append(f"{self.name} was already running")
        else:
            self.call(["start", self.name, "--hide"])
        self.wait_ip()
        if fresh:
            self.provision()
        return "running"

    def down(self) -> str:
        state = self.state()
        if state == "absent":
            raise Fail(f"{self.name} is absent; there is nothing to stop", 1)
        if state == "stopped":
            self.notes.append(f"{self.name} was already stopped")
        else:
            self.call(["stop", self.name])
        return "stopped"

    def tags(self) -> list:
        _, out, _ = self.call(["snapshot", "list", self.name, "--json"])
        if self.assume is not None:
            return self.assume.tags(self.name)
        try:
            rows = json.loads(out or "[]")
        except ValueError:
            raise Fail("utmctl snapshot list --json did not print JSON", 1)
        names = []
        for row in rows if isinstance(rows, list) else []:
            names.append(row.get("name", "") if isinstance(row, dict) else str(row))
        return names

    def snapshot(self, tag: str) -> str:
        state = self.state()
        if state == "absent":
            raise Fail(f"{self.name} is absent; run `ctlhq-env up` first", 1)
        if tag in self.tags():
            self.call(["snapshot", "overwrite", self.name, "--snapshot", tag])
            self.notes.append(f"replaced the earlier snapshot {tag}")
        else:
            self.call(["snapshot", "create", self.name, "--name", tag])
        return state

    def restore(self, tag: str) -> str:
        state = self.state()
        if state == "absent":
            raise Fail(f"{self.name} is absent; run `ctlhq-env up` first", 1)
        tags = self.tags()
        if tag not in tags:
            raise Fail(f"{self.name} has no snapshot {tag!r} (snapshots: {', '.join(tags) or 'none'})", 1)
        self.call(["snapshot", "restore", self.name, "--snapshot", tag])
        return state

    def exec_args(self, argv: list) -> list:
        return ["exec", self.name, "--cmd"] + argv

    def status(self) -> str:
        state = self.state()
        if state == "running":
            rc, out, _ = self.call(["ip-address", self.name], check=False)
            self.ip = out.strip().splitlines()[0] if rc == 0 and out.strip() else ""
        return state

    def list_states(self) -> dict:
        _, out, _ = self.call(["list"])
        if self.assume is not None:
            return {n: self.assume.machine_state(n) for n in self.assume.data["machines"]}
        found = {}
        for line in out.splitlines()[1:]:
            parts = line.split(None, 2)
            if len(parts) == 3:
                word = parts[1]
                found[parts[2].strip()] = "stopped" if word in self.STOPPED else ("running" if word == "started" else word)
        return found


class Local(Provider):
    binary = "local"

    def call(self, args: list, passthrough: bool = False, check: bool = True):
        argv = ["(this machine)"] + args
        if self.assume is not None:
            self.steps.append({"argv": argv, "exit": None})
            return 0, "", ""
        if not shutil.which(args[0]):
            self.steps.append({"argv": argv, "exit": 127})
            raise Fail(f"{args[0]} not found on PATH of this machine", 127)
        if passthrough:
            p = subprocess.run(args)
            out, err = "", ""
        else:
            p = subprocess.run(args, capture_output=True, text=True, stdin=subprocess.DEVNULL)
            out, err = p.stdout, p.stderr
        self.steps.append({"argv": argv, "exit": p.returncode})
        if check and p.returncode != 0:
            raise StepFailed(f"{show(args)} exited {p.returncode}" + (f": {err.strip()[-400:]}" if err.strip() else ""),
                             p.returncode)
        return p.returncode, out, err

    def host(self) -> str:
        return socket.gethostname()

    def up(self) -> str:
        self.notes.append(f"local provider: up does nothing; commands run on this machine ({self.host()})")
        return "running"

    def down(self) -> str:
        self.notes.append(f"local provider: down does nothing; this machine ({self.host()}) keeps running")
        return "running"

    def snapshot(self, tag: str) -> str:
        raise Fail("local provider cannot snapshot this machine; use a tart or utm recipe", 1)

    def restore(self, tag: str) -> str:
        raise Fail("local provider cannot restore this machine; use a tart or utm recipe", 1)

    def exec_args(self, argv: list) -> list:
        return argv

    def screenshot(self, out: Path) -> None:
        if self.assume is None and not shutil.which("screencapture"):
            raise Fail("screencapture not found on PATH of this machine (macOS only)", 127)
        if self.assume is None:
            out.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
        self.call(["screencapture", "-x", "-t", "png", str(out)])

    def status(self) -> str:
        return "running"

    def list_states(self) -> dict:
        return {}


REAL = {"tart": Tart, "utm": Utm, "local": Local}


class FakeState:
    def __init__(self, folder: Path) -> None:
        self.folder = folder
        self.path = folder / "state.json"
        self.data = {"machines": {}}
        if self.path.is_file():
            try:
                self.data = json.loads(self.path.read_text(encoding="utf-8"))
            except ValueError:
                raise Fail(f"{self.path} is not JSON; delete it to start over", 1)
            self.data.setdefault("machines", {})

    def machine_state(self, name: str) -> str:
        m = self.data["machines"].get(name)
        return m["state"] if m else "absent"

    def tags(self, name: str) -> list:
        m = self.data["machines"].get(name)
        return list(m.get("snapshots", [])) if m else []

    def as_tart(self, name: str) -> dict:
        found = {n: m["state"] for n, m in self.data["machines"].items()}
        for tag in self.tags(name):
            found[f"{name}-snap-{tag}"] = "stopped"
        return found

    def save(self) -> None:
        self.folder.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
        tmp = self.path.with_suffix(".tmp")
        tmp.write_text(json.dumps(self.data, indent=2, sort_keys=True) + "\n", encoding="utf-8")
        tmp.replace(self.path)

    def log(self, entry: dict) -> None:
        self.folder.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
        with open(self.folder / "calls.jsonl", "a", encoding="utf-8") as fh:
            fh.write(json.dumps(entry, sort_keys=True) + "\n")

    def script(self, op: str):
        p = self.folder / "script.json"
        if not p.is_file():
            return None
        try:
            data = json.loads(p.read_text(encoding="utf-8"))
        except ValueError:
            raise Fail(f"{p} is not JSON", 1)
        return data.get(op)


def result(op: str, provider: str, recipe: dict, **kw) -> dict:
    out = {"op": op, "provider": provider, "name": recipe["name"] if recipe else None, "exit": 0}
    out.update(kw)
    return out


def run_real(ctx: dict, op: str, recipe: dict, args: list, provider: str) -> dict:
    p = REAL[provider](recipe, ctx)
    res = result(op, provider, recipe, fake=False)
    try:
        if op == "up":
            res["state"] = p.up()
        elif op == "down":
            res["state"] = p.down()
        elif op == "snapshot":
            res["state"] = p.snapshot(args[0])
            res["tag"] = args[0]
        elif op == "restore":
            res["state"] = p.restore(args[0])
            res["tag"] = args[0]
        elif op == "exec":
            rc, out, err = p.exec(args)
            res["exit"] = rc
            if rc != 0:
                res["error"] = f"{show(args)} exited {rc} in {recipe['name']}"
            if ctx["json"]:
                res["stdout"], res["stderr"] = out, err
        elif op == "screenshot":
            p.screenshot(Path(args[0]))
            res["file"] = str(Path(args[0]).resolve())
        elif op == "status":
            res["state"] = p.status()
    except Fail as e:
        res.update(exit=e.code, error=e.msg)
    res["ip"] = p.ip
    res["steps"] = p.steps
    res["notes"] = p.notes
    return res


def plan_for(ctx: dict, op: str, recipe: dict, args: list, fake: FakeState):
    """The steps the recipe's real provider would take, given the fake state. Return (provider, steps, notes, error)."""
    real = recipe["provider"]
    p = REAL[real](recipe, ctx, assume=fake)
    try:
        if op in ("up", "down", "status"):
            getattr(p, op)()
        elif op in ("snapshot", "restore"):
            getattr(p, op)(args[0])
        elif op == "exec":
            p.call(p.exec_args(args), check=False)
        elif op == "screenshot":
            p.screenshot(Path(args[0]))
    except Fail as e:
        return real, p.steps, p.notes, e
    return real, p.steps, p.notes, None


def run_fake(ctx: dict, op: str, recipe: dict, args: list) -> dict:
    fake = FakeState(ctx["state"] / "fake")
    name = recipe["name"]
    before = fake.machine_state(name)
    real, steps, notes, error = plan_for(ctx, op, recipe, args, fake)
    res = result(op, "fake", recipe, fake=True, real_provider=real, state_file=str(fake.path),
                 plan=[show(s["argv"]) for s in steps], steps=[], notes=notes, ip="")
    scripted = fake.script(op)
    if error is None and op in ("exec", "screenshot") and before != "running":
        error = Fail(f"{name} is {before} (fake); run `ctlhq-env --provider fake up {name}` first", 1)
    if error is not None:
        res.update(exit=error.code, error=error.msg)
    elif op == "exec":
        s = scripted or {}
        res.update(exit=int(s.get("exit", 0)), stdout=str(s.get("stdout", "")), stderr=str(s.get("stderr", "")))
        if res["exit"] != 0:
            res["error"] = f"{show(args)} exited {res['exit']} in {name} (fake, scripted)"
    elif scripted is not None and int(scripted.get("exit", 0)) != 0:
        res.update(exit=int(scripted["exit"]), error=f"scripted failure for {op} (fake): exit {int(scripted['exit'])}")
    else:
        machines = fake.data["machines"]
        m = machines.get(name)
        if op == "up":
            if m is None:
                m = machines[name] = {"state": "stopped", "snapshots": [], "ip": f"192.0.2.{len(machines) + 9}"}
            m["state"] = "running"
            res["ip"] = m["ip"]
        elif op == "down":
            m["state"] = "stopped"
        elif op == "snapshot":
            if args[0] not in m["snapshots"]:
                m["snapshots"].append(args[0])
            res["tag"] = args[0]
        elif op == "restore":
            if m is None:
                raise Fail("fake state lost the machine", 1)
            res["tag"] = args[0]
        elif op == "screenshot":
            out = Path(args[0])
            out.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
            out.write_bytes(TINY_PNG)
            res["file"] = str(out.resolve())
        if m is not None and op == "status":
            res["ip"] = m["ip"] if m["state"] == "running" else ""
        fake.save()
    res["state"] = fake.machine_state(name)
    fake.log({"time": time.strftime("%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ", time.gmtime()), "op": op, "name": name,
              "args": args, "exit": res["exit"], "plan": res["plan"], "state_before": before,
              "state_after": res["state"]})
    return res


def cmd_list(ctx: dict) -> int:
    recipes = all_recipes(ctx["envs"])
    states: dict = {}
    provider = ctx["provider"]
    if provider == "fake":
        fake = FakeState(ctx["state"] / "fake")
        states = {r["name"]: fake.machine_state(r["name"]) for r in recipes}
    elif provider in ("tart", "utm"):
        holder = {"name": "-", "provider": provider, "guest": "linux", "network": "shared"}
        p = REAL[provider](holder, ctx)
        try:
            states = p.list_states()
        except Fail as e:
            print(f"ctlhq-env: {e.msg}", file=sys.stderr)
            return e.code
    elif provider == "local":
        states = {r["name"]: "running (this machine)" for r in recipes}
    rows = []
    for r in recipes:
        row = {k: r[k] for k in ("name", "provider", "guest", "image", "cpu", "memory_mb", "disk_gb",
                                 "network", "summary", "not_covered")}
        if provider:
            row["state"] = states.get(r["name"], "absent")
        rows.append(row)
    if ctx["json"]:
        print(json.dumps(rows, indent=2))
        return 0
    if provider == "fake":
        print("fake provider: states below are fake; no machine runs")
    width = max((len(r["name"]) for r in rows), default=4)
    iwidth = max((len(r["image"]) for r in rows), default=5)
    swidth = max((len(r.get("state", "")) for r in rows), default=0)
    for n, r in enumerate(rows, 1):
        state = f"  {r['state']:<{swidth}}" if provider else ""
        print(f"{n}. {r['name']:<{width}}  {r['provider']:<5}  {r['guest']:<7}  {r['image']:<{iwidth}}{state}  {r['summary']}")
    return 0


def print_text(res: dict, recipe: dict) -> None:
    op = res["op"]
    out = sys.stdout if res["exit"] == 0 and op != "exec" else sys.stderr
    if res.get("fake"):
        print(f"fake provider: no real machine was started or changed. Fake state: {res['state_file']}", file=out)
    if op == "exec" and res.get("fake"):
        sys.stdout.write(res.get("stdout", ""))
        sys.stderr.write(res.get("stderr", ""))
    if res["exit"] != 0:
        print(f"ctlhq-env: {res.get('error', 'failed')}", file=sys.stderr)
    elif op == "exec" and not res.get("fake"):
        return
    elif op == "exec":
        pass
    elif op == "screenshot":
        print(f"{res['name']}: screenshot written to {res['file']}", file=out)
    else:
        ip = f"  ip {res['ip']}" if res.get("ip") else ""
        tag = f"  snapshot {res['tag']}" if res.get("tag") else ""
        label = "fake" if res.get("fake") else res["provider"]
        print(f"{res['name']}: {res.get('state', '?')} ({label}){tag}{ip}", file=out)
    for note in res.get("notes", []):
        print(f"note: {note}", file=out)
    if res.get("steps"):
        print("steps:", file=out)
        for n, s in enumerate(res["steps"], 1):
            rc = s["exit"]
            print(f"  {n}. {show(s['argv'])}  exit {rc}", file=out)
    if res.get("fake"):
        plan = res.get("plan", [])
        print(f"A real run with {res['real_provider']} would take {len(plan)} step{'' if len(plan) == 1 else 's'}:", file=out)
        for n, line in enumerate(plan, 1):
            print(f"  {n}. {line}", file=out)
    if res["exit"] == 0 and op == "up":
        if recipe.get("snapshot_before_risky"):
            print(f"note: take a snapshot before risky tests: ctlhq-env snapshot {res['name']} <tag>", file=out)
        if recipe.get("log"):
            print(f"note: the machine's log is {recipe['log']}", file=out)
        print("does not cover: " + "; ".join(recipe["not_covered"]), file=out)
    if res["exit"] == 0 and op == "status" and recipe.get("log"):
        print(f"log: {recipe['log']}", file=out)


def parse_args(argv: list) -> dict:
    ctx = {"provider": None, "json": False, "envs": ROOT / "envs",
           "state": Path(os.environ.get("CTLHQ_ENV_STATE") or ROOT / ".local" / "env"),
           "out": None, "pos": [], "cmd": None}
    i = 0
    while i < len(argv):
        a = argv[i]
        if a == "--":
            ctx["cmd"] = argv[i + 1:]
            break
        if a in ("-h", "--help"):
            ctx["help"] = True
        elif a == "--json":
            ctx["json"] = True
        elif a in ("--provider", "--envs", "--state", "--out"):
            if i + 1 >= len(argv):
                raise Usage(f"{a} needs a value")
            v = argv[i + 1]
            i += 1
            if a == "--provider":
                if v not in PROVIDERS:
                    raise Usage(f"unknown provider {v!r} (use {', '.join(PROVIDERS)})")
                ctx["provider"] = v
            elif a == "--out":
                ctx["out"] = v
            else:
                ctx[a[2:]] = Path(v)
        elif a.startswith("-"):
            raise Usage(f"unknown option {a}")
        else:
            ctx["pos"].append(a)
        i += 1
    return ctx


def main(argv: list) -> int:
    try:
        ctx = parse_args(argv)
        if ctx.get("help"):
            print(__doc__.rstrip())
            return 0
        pos = ctx["pos"]
        if not pos:
            raise Usage("name a command")
        op, rest = pos[0], pos[1:]
        if op not in COMMANDS:
            raise Usage(f"unknown command {op!r}")
        if not ctx["envs"].is_dir():
            raise Fail(f"recipe folder {ctx['envs']} not found", 1)
        if op == "list":
            if rest or ctx["cmd"] is not None or ctx["out"]:
                raise Usage("list takes no arguments")
            return cmd_list(ctx)
        want = {"snapshot": 2, "restore": 2}.get(op, 1)
        if len(rest) != want:
            raise Usage(f"{op} needs {'NAME TAG' if want == 2 else 'NAME'}")
        if (ctx["cmd"] is not None) != (op == "exec"):
            raise Usage("exec needs `-- CMD`" if op == "exec" else f"{op} takes no `--` command")
        if op == "exec" and not ctx["cmd"]:
            raise Usage("exec needs a command after `--`")
        if (ctx["out"] is not None) != (op == "screenshot"):
            raise Usage("screenshot needs --out FILE" if op == "screenshot" else "--out belongs to screenshot")
        if want == 2 and not NAME_RE.match(rest[1]):
            raise Usage(f"bad TAG {rest[1]!r}: use letters, digits, dot, dash, underscore")
        recipe = load_recipe(ctx["envs"], rest[0])
        provider = ctx["provider"] or recipe["provider"]
        if provider == "tart" and recipe["guest"] == "windows":
            raise Usage("tart runs macOS and Linux guests only; this recipe needs utm")
        args = rest[1:] if want == 2 else []
        if op == "exec":
            args = ctx["cmd"]
        if op == "screenshot":
            args = [ctx["out"]]
        res = run_fake(ctx, op, recipe, args) if provider == "fake" else run_real(ctx, op, recipe, args, provider)
    except Usage as e:
        print(f"ctlhq-env: {e}", file=sys.stderr)
        print(USAGE, file=sys.stderr)
        return 2
    except Fail as e:
        print(f"ctlhq-env: {e.msg}", file=sys.stderr)
        return e.code
    if ctx["json"]:
        res.pop("_path", None)
        print(json.dumps(res, indent=2))
    else:
        print_text(res, recipe)
    return int(res["exit"])


if __name__ == "__main__":
    sys.exit(main(sys.argv[1:]))
